{
  "message": "The emulation run has no failures: the design wires up end to end, and every blocker is unfinished work, not something broken. The first one we can act on is the \"Raw and curated data\" bucket, which has no defined access. We need to decide which existing identity uploads the maintenance-records CSV, because I can then add a scoped read/write grant for that identity only. The other blockers, from ingestion through scoring, need product engineering (native generators for IoT Core, Glue and SageMaker), and a diagram edit can't fix that. Who uploads the synthetic maintenance CSV today: an existing AWS IAM role or user in this account, or a person who uploads it by hand? A minimal need would be read/write access for documents in this bucket only.",
